{"id":"jeiel","name":"Jeiel","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:jeiel"],"groups":["1. Also called JEHIEL"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Jeiel","text":"Snatched away by God. (1.) A descendant of Benjamin (1 Chr. 9:35; 8:29). (2.) One of the Levites who took part in praising God on the removal of the ark to Jerusalem (1 Chr. 16:5). (3.) 2 Chr. 29:13. A Levite of the sons of Asaph. (4.) 2 Chr. 26:11. A scribe. (5.) 1 Chr. 5:7. A Reubenite chief. (6.) One of the chief Levites, who made an offering for the restoration of the Passover by Josiah (2 Chr. 35:9). (7.) Ezra 8:13. (8.) Ezra 10:43."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H3273","lemma":"יְעִיאֵל","xlit":"Yᵉʻîyʼêl","gloss":"Jeiel, the name of six Israelites","kjv":"Jeiel, Jehiel","count":12,"share":1},{"strong":"H251","lemma":"אָח","xlit":"ʼâch","gloss":"a brother )","kjv":"another, brother; kindred, like, other","count":3,"share":0.25},{"strong":"H1121","lemma":"בֵּן","xlit":"bên","gloss":"a son , in the widest sense , etc.)","kjv":"afflicted, age, ite, ed one","count":5,"share":0.42}],"verses":["1Chr.5.7","1Chr.9.35","1Chr.11.44","1Chr.15.18","1Chr.15.21","1Chr.16.5","2Chr.20.14","2Chr.26.11","2Chr.29.13","2Chr.35.9","Ezra.8.13","Ezra.10.43"],"related":[{"id":"mattithiah","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.25,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"obed-edom","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.111,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"benaiah","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.103,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"zechariah-zecharias","type":"cooccur","shared":5,"jaccard":0.096,"why":"5 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"asaph","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.059,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"asahel","type":"lexical","strong":"H251","why":"both lead with אָח (H251)"},{"id":"azareel","type":"lexical","strong":"H251","why":"both lead with אָח (H251)"},{"id":"bethuel","type":"lexical","strong":"H251","why":"both lead with